# <claudes_code_comments>
# ** WHAT THIS FILE IS **
# The definition of branch triple-winners: THE THREE MEASURED WINNERS of round 4
# (2026-09-17-R4-RESULT-*.md, no-drop reading, solo on the new tip), and nothing else:
#     triple-pool           +7.27 %   3/4    the io_uring ring over the pread pool
#     triple-hitsfirst      +6.47 %   4/4    launch the resident experts before the miss reads land
#     triple-prefetch-pool  +2.28 %   4/4    the prefill prefetch read in chunks across a private pool
# It answers the navigator's question "why not combine pool and hitsfirst and prefetch-pool?"
# with a tree round 7 can measure. The line kinds are stack.manifest's (see the ten-lever
# stack-on-newtip.manifest on triple-all-fastest-newtip for the legend); the machinery is the
# same build_stack.sh / stack_resolve.py, copied onto this branch so it is self-contained.
#
# ** DEFAULTS **
# pool ON · hitsfirst ON (the lever's own default: DS4_CUDA_HITS_FIRST=0 turns it off) ·
# prefetch-pool ON. No patch line: nothing here is code that no lever carries. The prefetch
# victim order is the tip's own (`used` ascending, ds4_gpu_stream_expert_cache_prefetch);
# the sweep-aware comparator and DS4_CUDA_PREFETCH_SWEEP_ORDER belong to readahead-order,
# which this tree does not carry, so there is no region to gate.
#
# ** DERIVATION **
#   base      git rev-parse triple-tip-2026-09-16
#   shas      git rev-parse triple-<name>~1   (the code commit under each card commit; all
#                                              three branches are rebased onto the tip)
#   resolve   decided one hunk at a time, 2026-09-17, lane WINNERS, on a tree built lever by
#             lever (the survey's prefetch-pool numbering is taken on a theirs-throughout
#             hitsfirst tree and is NOT the numbering below: 30 ds4_cuda.cu hunks, not 28).
#
# ** THE RESOLUTION LEDGER - 49 hunks (hitsfirst 16, prefetch-pool 33): ours 14 · theirs 19 · both 3 · hand 13 **
#   (derive: grep '^resolve' | awk '{print $4}' | sed 's/:.*//' | sort | uniq -c)
#   hitsfirst Makefile 00          list union: the hits-first test beside pool's two
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 05       pool's dispatch_start(pool,..) wrapper kept beside the staged
#                                  entry points; both route to one staged body
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 08       hits-first's wait_stage wrapper + pool's whole io_uring ring
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 10       hits-first's miss mask + pool's claim ledger + stats_on gating
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 12       THE CLAIM-LEDGER HUNK, and it is NEEDED with hitsfirst ON:
#                                  when hits-first takes the batch the pool owns the reads and
#                                  cuda_hits_first_wait drops any slot whose bytes do not land,
#                                  so every claim is committed there - or pool's RAII ledger
#                                  would withdraw the slots on return while the reads are still
#                                  in flight (same shape as the newtip stack's hitsfirst 13)
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 13       ledger commit on the plain path + hits-first's stats gating
#   prefetch-pool Makefile 01 02   list unions
#   prefetch-pool ds4_cuda.cu 00   both comment paragraphs; the ceiling is 32u (the config
#                                  header static_asserts it)
#   prefetch-pool ds4_cuda.cu 04   private-fd pool fields + cfg-resolved enabled()/limit() +
#                                  the zero-arg cuda_expert_pread_pool_enabled() the ring calls
#   prefetch-pool ds4_cuda.cu 05   private descriptors + pool's once-per-fd rejection check
#   prefetch-pool ds4_cuda.cu 12   task_run(pool, ctx, t) + hits-first's stage_done broadcast +
#                                  prefetch-pool's drained_at stamp
#   prefetch-pool ds4_cuda.cu 17   the staged entry points + the unclamped-limit worker count
#   Every `ours` on prefetch-pool 03 20 21 23 25-28 keeps hits-first's staging and pool's
#   ledger where the lever's diff only re-contexted the tip; every `theirs` on 07-11 13-16
#   18 19 22 is the private-fd plumbing the lever is; 06 ours keeps pool's rejected-fd store;
#   10 theirs takes no_fadvise gating (no pagecache lever here, so no discard-then-drop order).
#
# ** THE CHECK **
#   bash build_stack.sh winners.manifest --check <HEAD of triple-winners>
#   ⚠ NOT COMPILED FOR CUDA. Assembled on a Mac with no nvcc; `make` here builds the Metal
#   target only, which never sees ds4_cuda.cu. The first Spark build is the real gate.
# </claudes_code_comments>

base        12997e9c84b39258f28781b808d18ea0069af2ac
paths       *.c *.h *.cu *.cuh *.inc Makefile tests/ cuda/ speed-bench/*.c gguf-tools/
lever-base  12997e9c84b39258f28781b808d18ea0069af2ac

